# Self-hosted Supabase docker environment (models the committed `docker/.env` of a self-hosted
# deployment). Every value here is FAKE.

# PLANTED BUG (P-SB-DEFAULT-JWT-SECRET): the well-known DEFAULT self-hosted JWT secret, shipped
# verbatim in Supabase's docker-compose template. Left unrotated, every anon/service_role JWT is
# forgeable by anyone — the secret is public knowledge. gitleaks supabase-default-jwt-secret → high.
JWT_SECRET=your-super-secret-jwt-token-with-at-least-32-characters-long

# NEGATIVE (N-SB-JWT-ROTATED): a rotated, random JWT secret — the correct state. It is NOT the
# published default string, so the default-secret rule does not match. (A high-entropy literal may
# draw a generic review-tier hit, triaged out; it is never a free-count finding.)
ANON_JWT_SECRET=Rk7pQ2mZ9vXcW8sNdLhGfYtAe4Uo1BxJ3wEr5Ty6Ui8Op0As2Df4Gh6Jk8Lz
